repoman (1.3.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * Support -o/--distro NAME:RELEASE (e.g. debian:bookworm); store mirror
    state per release under ~/.config/repoman/lrm/DISTRO/RELEASE/. Auto-append
    host VERSION_CODENAME or VERSION_ID when no release is given; migrate
    legacy flat or unversioned state into the host release path.
  * Seed archive and vault mirrors for EOL releases: Debian archive.debian.org
    and debian-archive mirrors, Ubuntu old-releases.ubuntu.com, CentOS
    vault.centos.org; probe URLs follow the specified suite or releasever.
  * Add drm (Docker repo manager): list, benchmark, and apply registry mirrors
    to /etc/docker/daemon.json via python3; built-in Docker Hub and Chinese
    registry seeds; drm(1), bash completion, and gettext catalog.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Mon, 13 Jul 2026 04:16:00 +0800

repoman (1.2.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * Add -o/--distro NAME and -l/--list-distros; support 76 distribution
    names (Debian, RPM, Arch families, including uos, kylin, openeuler,
    deepin, openkylin, tencentos, ctyunos, alinux, and others).
  * Store mirror state per distribution under
    ~/.config/repoman/lrm/DISTRO/; migrate legacy flat files into the
    host-distribution directory only.
  * Seed built-in mirrors per distribution profile with correct upstream
    and Chinese mirror URLs; use distro-specific bwtest probe paths.
  * Show mirror status on list: emoji by default (in use, failed, fastest,
    ok, untested); ASCII marks with list -c/--char (* x + v ?).
  * Record fastest mirror from pingtest/bwtest in DISTRO/preferred.
  * Update bash completion for distro options, apply flags, and list marks.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Mon, 13 Jul 2026 03:02:00 +0800

repoman (1.1.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * Add CSI-colored logging by verbosity level when terminfo supports it.
  * Refactor user-visible strings to gettext; configure LOCALEDIR via Meson
    with lookup order: source po/, build po/, installed localedir.
  * Translate CLI help and messages (zh_CN, zh_TW, and other LINGUAS).
  * Hand-translated man pages and READMEs (zh_CN); CLI catalogs via gettext.
  * Rewrite README.md and README-zh.md for the bash-only lrm tool.

